    {
      "id": "64",
      "type": "writeup",
      "attributes": {
        "id": 64,
        "body_ja": null,
        "body": "<p><span data-gp-id='714'>誰（だれ）</span> is a <span data-term='代名詞・だいめいし'>substitute noun</span> that is used in Japanese to describe unknown people. Due to Japanese particles behaving in very specific ways, <span data-gp-id='714'>誰（だれ）</span> will be translated differently depending on the particle that follows it.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><span data-gp-id='714'>誰（だれ）</span><span data-gp-id='10'>が</span>・<span data-gp-id='714'>誰（だれ）</span><span data-gp-id='36'>で</span>・<span data-gp-id='714'>誰（だれ）</span><span data-gp-id='32'>に</span>・<span data-gp-id='714'>誰（だれ）</span><span data-gp-id='21'>を</span> (who), <span data-gp-id='714'>誰（だれ）</span><span data-gp-id='6'>の</span> (whose), <span data-gp-id='714'>誰（だれ）</span><span data-gp-id='8'>か</span> (somebody), <span data-gp-id='714'>誰（だれ）</span><span data-gp-id='4'>も</span> (any/everybody).</p>\r\n\r\n<ul class='writeup-examples--holder'>\r\n<li data-study-question='154941'>\r\n<li data-study-question='154942'>\r\n<li data-study-question='154943'>\r\n<li data-study-question='154944'>\r\n<li data-study-question='154945'>\r\n<li data-study-question='154946'>\r\n<li data-study-question='154947'></ul>\r\n\r\n<section class='caution'><h4>Caution</h4>\r\n<p>Depending on the style of polite speech, there are several different words that will be used to indicate an unknown person. どなた is used in <span data-term='尊敬語・そんけいご'>honorific language</span>, while どちらさま is used in <span data-term='丁寧語・ていねいご'>polite speech</span>.</p></section>"
      }
